  "id": "Compound::DB00706 - Gene::150",
  "verbalization": "Tamsulosin, a selective alpha-1 adrenergic receptor antagonist, is shown to bind to Adra1d, a variant of the alpha-1 adrenergic receptor. This binding is linked to the participation of Adra1d in Alpha-adrenergic Receptor Activity, which is then participated by Adra2a. Similarly, Tamsulosin binds to Adra1d, which participates in Adrenergic Receptor Activity, and this activity is also participated by Adra2a. These pathways suggest that Tamsulosin may influence Adra2a through its interaction with Adra1d, which is involved in adrenergic signaling. The evidence supports a mechanism where Tamsulosin modulates Adra2a via Adra1d, potentially affecting adrenergic receptor function. The consistent involvement of Adra1d in both Alpha- and Adrenergic Receptor Activity indicates a shared role in receptor-mediated signaling, reinforcing the proposed relationship between Tamsulosin and Adra2a.",
